        "original_id": "1f1eabc2-5c9e-5182-99c4-200ba6ce71d0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sandy River Plantation, Rangeley, Franklin County, Maine\n- Products: Saddleback Maine ski resort\n- Places: Saddleback Mountain\n- Concepts: ski area size metrics, topographic prominence\n\nFacts:\n- Saddleback Mountain is located in Sandy River Plantation, Franklin County, Maine, near the resort town of Rangeley.\n- Saddleback Mountain is one of the highest mountains in Maine and one of fourteen mountains in the state with more than 2,000 feet of topographic prominence.\n- Saddleback Maine is a ski resort on the northwestern slopes of Saddleback Mountain in Sandy River Plantation, near Rangeley, Maine.\n- Saddleback Mountain is the site of the Saddleback Maine ski resort.\n- Saddleback Maine is the third largest ski area in Maine by number of trails, number of lifts, snowmaking percentage, vertical drop, and skier days.\n- Saddleback Maine has 66 trails, 5 lifts, 85% snowmaking coverage, and a 2,000-foot vertical drop.",
